      "checked_at": "2026-10-18T02:50:45+00:00",
      "text": "Bonjour ! - Lawless French - Online French Learning French lessons and language tools from Laura K Lawless Chatbot Cool Tools Pronommeur Subjunctivisor Verb Deconjugator Verb Tables Daily Practice FAQ French 101 P w LF Search Welcome! About LKL Beyond Lawless French French Essentials French for Beginners Frequently Asked Questions Independent Study Lessons by Level Log in Online Learning Tips Relearning French Sitemap Subscribe to Lawless French Support LF Teachers’ Tips and Tools The Fine Print Ad and Affiliate Disclosure Privacy Policy What’s New Workbook ✏️ Bonjour ! et bienvenue à Lawless French , a free resource for students, teachers, and lovers of the beautiful French language. New here? Take a look at my Welcome Page , or just scroll to start exploring some of the most popular features on the site. If you’re a regular visitor, click to discover what’s new . À bientôt ! Lessons by Level Lessons and exercises ranked according to six levels of language proficiency. French 101 Self-study course with lessons, cultural tips, listening exercises, and quizzes. Daily Practice Ideas Regular practice is key – just 15 minutes a day can make all the difference. Grammar Parts of speech, sentence structure, conjugations, and all the other rules. Pronunciation Letters, letter combinations, liaisons, accents, contractions, and more. Vocabulary Themed vocab lists + wordy lessons: synonyms, prefixes, abbreviations… Quizzes and Tests Assorted quizzes, online proficiency test, and info about official certification. The Subjunctivisor! Does [ insert verb | expression | conjunction ] require the subjunctive? Verb Tables 1,600+ French verbs conjugated into all the simple tenses and moods. Langua French Chat Practice speaking French any time of day or night with a human-like AI. Progress with Lawless French Find your level to get a personalized study plan and learning resources. Frantastique Story-based learning with daily lessons, dialogues, historical notes, and comics. French Language Skills Reading Listening Speaking Writing French proficiency test by Stay up to date with Lawless French Questions about French? Visit the Progress with Lawless French Q+A forum to get help from native French speakers and fellow learners. Support Lawless French This free website is created with love and a great deal of work. If you love it, please consider making a one-time or monthly donation . What’s New at Lawless French? Faire le point Assess your understanding of the French expression faire le point by reviewing this lesson. Comparatives Quiz - Lecture ou Télé ? Test yourself on comparatives with this fill-in-the-blanks test: Lecture ou Télé ? Note: You must be logged into your Progress with Lawless French account to take this test. If you don’t have one, sign up – it’s free! Learn French Online Is it possible to learn French online? Sure, at least to a certain extent. Here are some tips and tools to help you learn French on your own. Informal Pronouns Pronoun usage and pronunciation varies greatly between formal and informal French. Much of what you learn at school is formal and doesn’t reflect how French is actually spoken. If you want to sound more French in informal situations—not to mention understand what you hear—you need to be aware of these pronoun differences. Fromage français Le fromage est l’une des denrées les plus typiques de la France, mais que savez-vous à son propos ? Aujourd’hui je vous présente le monde fascinant du fromage français. Mon œil ! No need to suspend your disbelief with this lesson on the French expression mon œil . Free newsletter Please leave this field empty Lawless French is sent every Tuesday and Friday with the latest lessons and features. Email * Please check your email and click the link to confirm your subscription - merci ! © 2026 Lawless French. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy Created by Laura K Lawless , author of French Workbook for Dummies and French Essentials for Dummies Hosted by PeoplesHost Cassie by ThemeMeme Subscribe to the free Lawless French newsletter Get new lessons and features in your inbox 2x per week Grammar, vocab, pronunciation lessons Expression of the week Quizzes and exercises Listening and reading comprehension Cultural content Occasional product reviews + offers Subscribe Bonjour ! Lawless French is a free website . Please disable your ad-blocker or donate to support my work . BONUS Donate US$5 / month to unlock le Mot du jour . I'll make a donation I'll disable my ad-blocker",
